{
  "summary": "The image-only, multiprofile ResNet50 model with avgpool achieved validation accuracy 0.3275 and F1 0.2884, above the prior image-only single-profile ResNet50 baseline of 0.2079 accuracy but far below the strongest RNA multiprofile scVI results near 0.65 accuracy. This initial observation suggests that adding multiprofile avgpool aggregation to the image-only ResNet setting yields a modest validation improvement over the single-profile image baseline, though the comparison does not isolate the effect of multiprofile modeling from avgpool aggregation. It remains uncertain whether the residual weakness reflects limited image signal, an inadequate ResNet50 representation, or the absence of RNA/fusion, so further investment in ResNet-based multimodal variants is not yet clearly justified."
}

